WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.229 --> 00:00:03.451
So the clowns over at Fox News are just that

00:00:03.451 --> 00:00:08.990
absolutely thrilled that we live in a country
where people are free to work multiple jobs

00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:13.419
because one job doesn't give them a stable,
a standard of living.

00:00:13.419 --> 00:00:20.100
There's this concept called freedom from versus
freedom too that exists in political philosophy

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.260
and it relates to positive and negative freedoms.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:28.890
Okay, so positive liberty is the freedom to
do something and negative liberty is the freedom

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:33.440
from being stopped by other people from doing
something.

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:38.300
So the point is there's different types of
liberty and sometimes the freedom to do something

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:42.629
is actually only relevant because there's
a lack of freedom somewhere else.

00:00:42.629 --> 00:00:43.629
So here's an example.

00:00:43.629 --> 00:00:49.559
If I say it's great to have the freedom in
the United States to work for whichever company

00:00:49.559 --> 00:00:54.200
gives you the best health insurance, a counterpoint
would be, hold on a second.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:59.429
It's terrible to lack the freedom in the United
States to be able to just work whatever job

00:00:59.429 --> 00:01:06.000
is the most rewarding job without being constrained
by worrying about losing your health insurance.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.630
That's the way I would see it.

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:08.630
Okay.

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:09.630
This gets us to Fox News.

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:13.320
Now, if I said to you, if you look at the
numbers of people in the United States who

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:18.320
are working multiple jobs, is that a form
of freedom to work as many jobs as you want?

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:22.670
Or is that actually a reflection of the lack
of freedom that stagnant wages and a lack

00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:28.540
of living wages place on people and force
them into having to work multiple jobs?

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:34.220
I consider the working multiple jobs thing,
an indicator of the lack of freedom that too

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:38.890
many workers in the United States experience,
which gets us to the Fox News perspective

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:45.930
on this issue where absolute and total farcical
clowns, Pete Heg, Seth and Ainslie Earhart

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:47.110
are just gushing.

00:01:47.110 --> 00:01:52.010
They're literally thanking God about how wonderful
it is that we live in a country where people

00:01:52.010 --> 00:01:53.420
can work multiple jobs.

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:59.870
Uh, uh, and it's, it's mind blowing that this
is actually an analysis that resonates with

00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:01.590
millions of people in this country.

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:02.590
Take a look.

00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:03.590
Yeah.

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:05.290
You know what Kamel Harris says is so, so
disingenuous.

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:09.030
For most of my life, I've worked two or three
or four of jobs

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:10.140
of sources of income.

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:11.140
Okay.

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:12.299
Today, you can do that more flexibly.

00:02:12.299 --> 00:02:15.879
How many people do you know who do something
and then maybe in their free time they drive

00:02:15.879 --> 00:02:18.890
an Uber or they do something else to bring
in extra cash?

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:22.819
Thank God we live in the kind of country where
we have the innovation and flexibility where

00:02:22.819 --> 00:02:25.560
you can bring in money from different places,
do different things.

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:29.260
When I'm in an Uber and you talk to them,
you get to know on many of them do say they're

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:32.849
doing this to make a little extra money and
then we start talking about how much extra

00:02:32.849 --> 00:02:36.960
do you monitor fast do you make a week and
it's enough to pay for their kids to take

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:38.060
an extra swim class.

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:41.550
This one guy told me, or it's enough to put
a little bit of money aside for their kids

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:42.550
to go to college.

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:43.689
I love those types of people.

00:02:43.689 --> 00:02:45.030
My Dad worked several jobs.

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:47.370
If he had the opportunity to make a little
extra, he would.

00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:48.769
These people are truly sick.

00:02:48.769 --> 00:02:55.400
These, I mean it's, it's not inspiring that
so many people have to work second jobs and

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:56.450
third jobs.

00:02:56.450 --> 00:03:00.069
It would be inspiring to live in a country
where people didn't have to do that.

00:03:00.069 --> 00:03:01.069
Right.

00:03:01.069 --> 00:03:07.389
This is like those supposedly heartwarming,
inspirational stories about how great Americans

00:03:07.389 --> 00:03:13.239
are because when little Jimmy needed a prosthetic
leg because of a medical condition, Jimmy's

00:03:13.239 --> 00:03:18.790
classmates and teachers came together to fundraise
and do bake sales to raise money.

00:03:18.790 --> 00:03:20.409
What a great country.

00:03:20.409 --> 00:03:21.730
No, no.

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:27.609
It's disgusting that one of the richest countries
in the world makes the reality one where Jimmy

00:03:27.609 --> 00:03:34.060
couldn't just get the prosthetic leg and needed
money from his classmates and from teachers

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:38.029
and from the parents of classmates buying
muffins at a bake sale.

00:03:38.029 --> 00:03:39.029
It's backwards.

00:03:39.029 --> 00:03:41.160
Okay, and I actually want to go further.

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:46.500
This multiple job status quo that's so common
actually reinforces the system we have, I've

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:51.299
talked about this in my segments about types
of activism that go beyond just signing a

00:03:51.299 --> 00:03:54.090
petition or calling your elected official.

00:03:54.090 --> 00:04:00.769
I've said before, corporations have huge disproportionate
control over our systems, the legal system,

00:04:00.769 --> 00:04:03.879
the judicial system, media, everything.

00:04:03.879 --> 00:04:09.799
They maintain control in part by making sure
that there's a system in which the average

00:04:09.799 --> 00:04:15.889
person doesn't go protest, doesn't demand
change, doesn't participate in strategic defaults

00:04:15.889 --> 00:04:17.930
or mass rallies in urban centers.

00:04:17.930 --> 00:04:21.840
And one of the best ways to make sure people
don't do that, that people don't protest and

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:27.560
people don't demand change is if they can't
even miss a day of work because that would

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:33.110
be two or three jobs that they might get fired
from or they can't miss a day of work because

00:04:33.110 --> 00:04:37.180
they can't buy food if they miss that day
of work.

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:42.810
That's a really great way to make sure people
don't show up and actually protest and demand

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:43.810
real change.

00:04:43.810 --> 00:04:49.560
And if you're in a situation where you even
need multiple jobs, then you are very unlikely

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:54.570
to have the wherewithal and resources to go
and protest and demand changes to the system

00:04:54.570 --> 00:04:57.130
that caused you to need two or three jobs
in the first place.

00:04:57.130 --> 00:05:02.900
This is a self reinforcing feedback loop and
I mean, listen, I don't know the Fox News

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:05.720
hosts who said it's just so inspiring to live
in a country.

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:09.440
Thank God we in a country where people can
work 10 jobs if that's what they want to do,

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:11.050
they may be useful idiots.

00:05:11.050 --> 00:05:15.460
They may be a actual cogs in the wheel deliberately
reinforcing the system.

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:16.460
It doesn't really matter.

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:17.460
Okay.

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:21.980
The effect is that they are reinforcing the
system that big corporations have already

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:24.971
done a pretty damn good job at reinforcing
really disturbing and disgusting stuff.

